  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "circuits",
      "claim": "providers.Runtime keeps its per-provider circuit breakers in one llmgw-core execution.HealthTracker configured from each provider's threshold and cooldown, with no failure window and Retry-After ignored, read by a gateway Observe that fails circuit failures, succeeds other invocation errors and ignores errors that never reached the upstream. The resilience wrapper's retry loops, the circuit-open 503 and their timing are unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/policy.go and runtime.go; circuit tests pinned before the change"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "router-execute",
      "claim": "All five router failover chains walk their candidates with execution.Execute; each chain's advance rule reaches Execute as the failure's classification, so the Messages chains still move past build, configuration and adapter failures. Endpoints, policy gates, translation-loss routing, affinity, compatibility filtering and telemetry stay product code. Streams commit when they open, as before, and cancellation keeps each chain's own context rules.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/router/failover.go; failover_boundary_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fixtures",
      "claim": "The M0 characterization fixtures, including failover-before-output and failover-after-output streams, pass unchanged, as do the router tests and the 115-case classification parity test; tests pinning the circuit breaker and the failover boundary pass on both the old and the new code.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/testdata unchanged; go/internal/router tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable, and router and providers pass under -count=10; coupling budgets are unchanged; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
